-- title:
--   Constructing all balanced terminal-completion masks
-- statement:
--   Let a global output have $J$ rows of size $2h$ in blocks of width $512h$, and fix $k\le J$ and an arbitrary prefix list $u$. Let $Q$ be the union of output coordinates in blocks $k,\ldots,J-1$, and let $L_u,R_u$ be the prefix endpoint sets, using empty rows when the list is missing entries. Enumerate all $t=(J-k)h$ element subsets $T_i$ of $Q$; their number is $N=\binom{2(J-k)h}{(J-k)h}$.
--
--   Reserve $N$-cell arrays at $m,a,b$ with $m+N\le a$, $a+N\le b$, $b+N\le w$. For $L=J(512h)$, assume $w+2L+2\le S\le W$, $2^{L+1}\le W$, and $d+L+3\le D$. The fixed program returns zero and writes
--   $$\nu(a+i)=\operatorname{mask}(L_u\cup T_i),\qquad\nu(b+i)=\operatorname{mask}(R_u\cup(Q\setminus T_i)).$$
--   It preserves cells below $m$ and meets the defined terminal-mask budget.
--
--   This constructs the full balanced residual scan without requiring prefix validity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightReportingTerminalMasks.lean#L77-L114

